          "text": "$f\\left(x\\right)=3\\left(x-a\\right)\\left(x-b\\right)\\left(x-c\\right)$   \nThe function f is defined by the given equation, where a, b, and c are distinct constant. When a &lt; x &lt; b, the value of f(x) is positive. The graph of y= f(x) in the xy-plane contains the point (r, s), where r and s are constants. If s = 8, which of the following could be true?  \nⅠ. $r\\lt a\\ \\ \\ b\\lt r\\lt a\\ \\ r\\gt c$  \n$r\\lt a\\ \\ \\ b\\lt r\\lt a\\ \\ r\\gt c$  \n$r\\lt a\\ \\ \\ b\\lt r\\lt a\\ \\ r\\gt c$"
        }
